              highlighted: ["E","AE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then {AE} and {ED} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: TERMS,
              highlighted: ["AE","ED"] },
            { text: "the square on {AE} is greater than the square on {ED}",
              visible: TERMS,
              highlighted: ["AE","ED"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable with {AE},",
              visible: TERMS,
              highlighted: ["AE"] },
            { text: "and the lesser term {ED} is commensurable in length with {AB}.",
              visible: TERMS,
              highlighted: ["ED","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AD a second binomial", ref: "X.Def.II.2" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {ED} at {F},",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["ED","F"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "F", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and apply to {AE} the rectangle {AG} by {GE}",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AE","AG","GE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "equal to the square on {EF} and deficient by a square figure.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GE","EF"] },
            { text: "Then {AG} is commensurable in length with {GE}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG, GE commensurable", ref: "X.17" }] },
            { text: "Draw {GH}, {EK}, and {FL} through {G}, {E}, and {F} parallel to {AB} and {CD}.",
              visible: PAR,
              highlighted: ["GH","EK","FL"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "GH",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "EK",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FL",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "AH",   name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "HGEK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Construct the square {SN} equal to the parallelogram {AH},",
              visible: SQ1,
              highlighted: ["AH","SPNM"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "S",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "SPNM", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and the square {NQ} equal to {GK},",
              visible: SQ2,
              highlighted: ["HGEK","NOQR"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "NOQR", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and place them so that {MN} is in a straight line with {NO}.",
              visible: SQ2,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO"] },
            { text: "Then {RN} is also in a straight line with {NP}.",
              visible: SQ3,
              highlighted: ["NR","PN"] },
            { text: "Complete the square {SQ}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["SQ"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "SQ", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "It is then manifest from what was proved before that {MR} is a mean proportional between {SN} and {NQ}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MR","SPNM","NOQR"] },
            { text: "and equals {EL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MR","EL"] },
            { text: "and that is the side of the area {AC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MO","ABCDh"] },
            { text: "It is now to be proved that {MO} is a first bimedial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MO"] },
            { text: "Since {AE} is commensurable in length with {ED}, while {ED} is commensurable with {AB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","ED","AB"] },
            { text: "therefore {AE} is incommensurable with {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE, AB incommensurable", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "Since {AG} is commensurable with {EG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GE"] },
            { text: "therefore {AE} is also commensurable with each of the straight lines {AG} and {GE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","AG","GE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE commensurable with AG, GE", ref: "X.15" }] },
            { text: "But {AE} is incommensurable in length with {AB}, therefore {AG} and {GE} are also incommensurable with {AB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","AG","GE","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG, GE incommensurable with AB", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {BA} and {AG}, and {BA} and {GE}, are pairs of rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AG","GE"] },
            { text: "so that each of the rectangles {AH} and {GK} is medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AH","HGEK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AH, GK medial", ref: "X.21" }] },
            { text: "Hence, each of the squares {SN} and {NQ} is medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["SPNM","NOQR"] },
            { text: "Therefore {MN} and {NO} are also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO"] },
            { text: "Since {AG} is commensurable in length with {GE}, therefore {AH} is also commensurable with {GK},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG","GE","AH","HGEK"] },
            { text: "that is, {SN} is commensurable with {NQ}, that is, the square on {MN} with the square on {NO}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["SPNM","NOQR","MN","NO"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG : GE = AH : GK", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "AH, GK commensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Since {AE} is incommensurable in length with {ED}, while {AE} is commensurable with {AG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","ED","AG"] },
            { text: "and {ED} is commensurable with {EF}, therefore {AG} is incommensurable with {EF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ED","EF","AG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG, EF incommensurable", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "so that {AH} is also incommensurable with {EL}, that is, {SN} is incommensurable with {MR},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AH","EL","SPNM","MR"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG : EF = AH : EL", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "AH, EL incommensurable", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "that is, {PN} with {NR}, that is, {MN} is incommensurable in length with {NO}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["PN","NR","MN","NO"] },
            { text: "But {MN} and {NO} were proved to be both medial and commensurable in square,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO"] },
            { text: "therefore {MN} and {NO} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO"] },
            { text: "I say next that they also contain a rational rectangle.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO","MR"] },
            { text: "Since {DE} is, by hypothesis, commensurable with each of the straight lines {AB} and {EF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ED","AB","EF"] },
            { text: "therefore {EF} is also commensurable with {EK}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EF","EK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EF, EK commensurable", ref: "X.12" }] },
            { text: "And each of them is rational, therefore {EL}, that is, {MR} is rational,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EF","EK","EL","MR"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EL rational", ref: "X.19" }] },
            { text: "and {MR} is the rectangle {MN} by {NO}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MR","MN","NO"] },
            { text: "But, if two medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a rational rectangle are added together,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN","NO"] },
            { text: "then the whole is irrational and is called a first bimedial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MO"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "first bimedial", ref: "X.37" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {MO} is a first bimedial straight line.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MO"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if an area is contained by a rational straight line and the second binomial,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCDh","AB","AD"] },
            { text: "then the side of the area is the irrational straight line which is called a first bimedial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MO"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.55") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VI.1":       "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.Def.II.2": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.II.2/",
        "X.11":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.12":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX12/",
        "X.13":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.17":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX17/",
        "X.19":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX19/",
        "X.21":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX21/",
        "X.37":       "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX37/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Bisect {ED} at {F}, and apply to {AE} the rectangle {AG} by {GE} equal to the square on {EF} and deficient by a square figure.  Then {AG} is commensurable in length with {GE}. [!just X.17]

Draw {GH}, {EK}, and {FL} through {G}, {E}, and {F} parallel to {AB} and {CD}.  Construct the square {SN}  equal to the parallelogram {AH}, and the square {NQ} equal to {GK}, and place them so that {MN} is in a straight line with {NO}.  Then {RN} is also in a straight line with {NP}. Complete the square {SQ}.

It is then manifest from what was proved before that {MR} is a mean proportional between {SN} and {NQ} and equals {EL}, and that is the side of the area {AC}.

It is now to be proved that {MO} is a first bimedial straight line.

Since {AE} is commensurable in length with {ED}, while {ED} is commensurable with {AB}, therefore {AE} is incommensurable with {AB}. [!just X.13]

Since {AG} is commensurable with {EG}, therefore {AE} is also commensurable with each of the straight lines {AG} and {GE}. [!just X.15]

But {AE} is incommensurable in length with {AB}, therefore {AG} and {GE} are also incommensurable with {AB}. [!just X.13]

Therefore {BA} and {AG}, and {BA} and {GE}, are pairs of rational straight lines commensurable in square only, so that each of the rectangles {AH} and {GK} is medial. [!just X.21]

Hence, each of the squares {SN} and {NQ} is medial.  Therefore {MN} and {NO} are also medial.

Since {AG} is commensurable in length with {GE}, therefore {AH} is also commensurable with {GK}, that is, {SN} is commensurable with {NQ}, that is, the square on {MN} with the square on {NO}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

Since {AE} is incommensurable in length with {ED}, while {AE} is commensurable with {AG}, and {ED} is commensurable with {EF}, therefore {AG} is incommensurable with {EF},  so that {AH} is also incommensurable with {EL}, that is, {SN} is incommensurable with {MR}, that is, {PN} with {NR}, that is, {MN} is incommensurable in length with {NO}. [!just X.13; VI.1; X.11]

But {MN} and {NO} were proved to be both medial and commensurable in square, therefore {MN} and {NO} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only.

I say next that they also contain a rational rectangle.

Since {DE} is, by hypothesis, commensurable with each of the straight lines {AB} and {EF}, therefore {EF} is also commensurable with {EK}. [!just X.12]

And each of them is rational, therefore {EL}, that is, {MR} is rational, and {MR} is the rectangle {MN} by {NO}. [!just X.19]

But, if two medial straight lines commensurable in square only and containing a rational rectangle are added together, then the whole is irrational and is called a first bimedial straight line. Therefore {MO} is a first bimedial straight line. [!just X.37]

Therefore, *if an area is contained by a rational straight line and the second binomial, then the side of the area is the irrational straight line which is called a first bimedial.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
